==English==

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|pathology|of an illness|lang=en}} [[transmit|Transmitted]] from one person to another, usually through the air breathed.
#: ''Cancer is not '''infectious'''.''
#: ''More '''infectious''' diseases like the flu are usually less potent.''
# {{context|pathology|of a person|lang=en}} Able to [[infect]] others.
#: ''Despite feeling better, the patient is still '''infectious'''.''
# {{context|of feelings and behaviour|lang=en}} Spreading quickly from one person to another.
#: ''Her enthusiasm for work can be really '''infectious'''.''
# {{context|informal|lang=en}} [[memorable|Memorable]] and invoking [[excitement]] or [[interest]].
#: ''Pop music is more '''infectious''' than elevator music.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|transmitted between persons as illness}} [[catching]], [[contagious]]
* {{sense|able to infect others}} [[contagious]]
* {{sense|spreading quickly between persons}} [[contagious]]
* {{sense|memorable and exciting}} [[catchy]], [[contagious]]

